  "notes": "Closed-score SATB: Soprano+Alto share the treble staff, Tenor+Bass share the bass staff. A correct conversion yields FOUR parts (Soprano, Alto, Tenor, Bass), each with its own notes; all three verses belong to the Soprano part (lyric numbers 1-3) and must stay attached to soprano notes, including melisma skips (e.g. \"pre - cious\" spans a slurred melisma). DAMAGE (crop): Image edges cut through the staves. Mild: tight crop 0.4 mm outside the staff ends (braces/brackets cut off). Scan: 0.8 mm cut into the staff starts (start barline and brace gone) and 0.8 mm off the staff ends (end/final barlines thinned or gone). Severe: cut up to 1.24 mm into the staff start (to just before the clef) and 10.3 mm off the ends (to just after the last notehead/stem), and the header (title, credits) is cropped away. Cut amounts were computed from the clean raster so that no clef, notehead, stem, accidental or lyric is removed. TRUTH LIMITATIONS: Barlines at system ends (incl. the final barline) may be partly or completely cut off - they are still present in the truth (barline positions are implied by the time signature). Severe: title/composer header text is not visible; ignore work-title/creators when scoring."
